author Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1785191283 -0700
committer Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1785202859 -0700

refactor: use chrono for fixed durations

State directly assigned duration constants in their natural units while preserving each destination type and value.
Apply the same direct conversion at simple call and comparison boundaries for peer bans, the scheduler limit, and wallet rebroadcast age.
Use named chrono duration types consistently within the peer ban actions rather than mixing them with literals such as `1h`.
The one-year action remains exactly 365 days.

For review, add this temporary test to `src/test/util_tests.cpp` to verify the conversions in this commit:

```cpp
BOOST_AUTO_TEST_CASE(util_chrono_fixed_duration_equivalence)
{
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(90 * 60, TicksSeconds(90min));
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(60 * 60, TicksSeconds(std::chrono::hours{1}));
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(24 * 60 * 60, TicksSeconds(std::chrono::days{1}));
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(7 * 24 * 60 * 60, TicksSeconds(std::chrono::weeks{1}));
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(30 * 24 * 60 * 60, TicksSeconds(std::chrono::days{30}));
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(31556952, TicksSeconds(std::chrono::years{1}));
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(8 * 60 * 60, TicksSeconds(8h));
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(std::chrono::seconds{60 * 60 * 24}.count(), std::chrono::seconds{std::chrono::days{1}}.count());
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(60 * 60 * 24 * 365, TicksSeconds(std::chrono::days{365}));
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(3600, TicksSeconds(1h));
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(5 * 60, TicksSeconds(5min));
}
```

Co-authored-by: janb84 <githubjanb.drainer976@passmail.net>

