qt: use chrono for time calculations

Name the assumed blocks per day directly in the prune backup estimate.
State the overlay animation, sample-window, and progress-rate intervals in their natural units, converting them at the Qt millisecond interfaces.

For review, add this temporary test to `src/test/util_tests.cpp` to verify the conversions in this commit:

```cpp
BOOST_AUTO_TEST_CASE(util_chrono_qt_equivalence)
{
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(24 * 60 * 60 / (10 * 60), std::chrono::days{1} / 10min);
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(300, count_milliseconds(300ms));
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(500 * 1000, count_milliseconds(500s));
    BOOST_REQUIRE_EQUAL(1000 * 3600, count_milliseconds(1h));
}
```

